"""Add final pilot findings while preserving the historical investigation."""
import json
from pilot import HERE


def main():
    summary=json.loads((HERE/'final-summary.json').read_text());stages=summary['stages'];core=stages['core']['groups'];advanced=stages['advanced_repeat']['groups'];fine=stages['fine_repeat']['groups'];novel=stages['novel']['groups']
    path=HERE.parent/'2026-09-10-comparison.md';original=path.read_text();title,body=original.split('\n',1)
    historical='## Original full-source investigation (before optimization pilot)'
    if historical in body:body=body.split(historical,1)[1]
    lines=[title,'','## Completed optimization pilot','','**ClickHouse can be substantially faster on these workloads with a suitable layout.** The completed bounded pilot found repeatable gains from typed time-sorted columns, compact historical metadata and exact hourly rollups with small granules. PostgreSQL was not queried again; comparisons use its saved results.','','The isolated cohort contains **13,711,369 rows**, preserving the original windows and their join lookback/follow-up. Across **2,616 benchmark requests**, every result matched the raw ClickHouse reference; all **1,192 observations with saved PostgreSQL evidence** matched it. Original candidates received two shuffled passes, each with one warmup and three measured repeats. Four new timestamp predicates—including a partial-hour range—also passed. Both query and condition caches were disabled.','','Core client medians below pool six measured samples from two passes on the same pilot:','','| Workload | Raw ClickHouse | Typed, time-sorted ClickHouse | Saved PostgreSQL |','|---|---:|---:|---:|']
    for case in ('event_counts/hour','feature_funnel/day','ab_outcome/day','feature_counts/day'):
        raw=core['raw/'+case]['median_client_ms'];typed=core['typed/'+case]['median_client_ms'];pg=summary['saved_postgres'][case]['median_client_ms']
        lines.append(f'| {case} | {raw:.1f} ms | {typed:.1f} ms | {pg:.1f} ms |')
    meta=advanced['metadata/metadata_join/day'];funnel=advanced['funnel/feature_funnel/day'];rollup=fine['rollup_fine/traffic_day/day'];fresh=novel['typed/event_counts/new_10h'];rawfresh=novel['raw/event_counts/new_10h']
    lines+=['',f"Independent advanced repeats confirmed compact metadata at **{meta['median_client_ms']:.1f} ms/day ({meta['speedup_vs_control']:.2f}× its same-pass typed control)**, a one-pass funnel at **{funnel['median_client_ms']:.1f} ms/day ({funnel['speedup_vs_control']:.2f}×)**, and fine exact traffic rollups at **{rollup['median_client_ms']:.1f} ms/day ({rollup['speedup_vs_control']:.2f}×)**. Coarse rollups regressed for hourly traffic; finer granules corrected that regression. Event/identity projections mostly gave small or absent gains, despite some being selected.",'',f"On the previously unqueried **September 7 10:00–11:00 UTC predicate**, typed event counts read **{fresh['median_read_rows']:,.0f} rows at {fresh['median_client_ms']:.1f} ms**, versus all **{rawfresh['median_read_rows']:,.0f} raw pilot rows at {rawfresh['median_client_ms']:.1f} ms**. This verifies pruning without condition-cache reuse. The partial-hour range passes raw/typed and join rewrites; rollups explicitly reject it.",'','Prefer the typed time-sorted layout as the broad candidate, compact metadata for the historical join, and fine exact rollups for stable hour-aligned summaries. Typed sorting, partitioning and extraction were tested together; their individual contributions are not isolated. Rollups/metadata are static backfills, with no live refresh or ingestion cost measured. All build/storage costs and negative findings are retained in the detailed report.','','**Limits:** this is an eight-day cohort, not a full 2.32-billion-row build or an equal-cost engine comparison. PostgreSQL hardware and a shared transactional snapshot are unavailable; saved equality covers 21 original case/window outputs. The new ClickHouse harness reuses HTTPS connections. Source-copy clustering differs from the original table, and typed storage omits full JSON payloads. The cohort contains no SSR events, so its SSR timings are not representative. Source DDL and part totals remain unchanged. An unresolved initial advanced-query-log gap is preserved; every independent repeated benchmark request has server logs.','','[Final detailed report](clickhouse-pilot/FINAL_REPORT.md) · [Machine-readable summary](clickhouse-pilot/final-summary.json) · [Per-query new-window evidence](clickhouse-pilot/novel-results.json) · [Final operational checks](clickhouse-pilot/final-verification.json)','','---','',historical,'',body.lstrip()]
    path.write_text('\n'.join(lines))
if __name__=='__main__':main()
